    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1: Number of thematic experts provided to cabinet for reconstruction to enable its mandated responsibilities of coordination, monitoring, oversight and implementation of standards for resilient recovery as defined in the Disaster Recovery Framework (DRF) 
2: 2 Standards and guidelines for resilient recovery in place to guide the recovery interventions in IDAI and Kenneth affected communities.
3: Sectoral coordination platform established and functional
4: Recovery Monitoring and Information Management System established and functional</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1: 5 experts (Recovery Planning, Coordination, Consultant, two Engineers) and 8 support technical staff provided to cabinet for reconstruction to enable its mandated responsibilities of coordination, monitoring, oversight and implementation of standards for resilient recovery as defined in the Disaster Recovery Framework (DRF). GREPOC composed the working team and continue with their role in the Pos Cyclone IDAI and Kenneth recovery programme.  
2: 1 Disaster Recovery Framework and Housing Reconstruction Guiding Programme (PALPOC) for resilient recovery coordinated and implemented to guide the recovery interventions in IDAI and Kenneth affected communities.
3:  Housing reconstruction coordination mechanism establish and functional. Mid-Term Evaluation of the Implementation of the Post Cyclone Recovery and Reconstruction Programme (PREPOC) concluded. GREPOC has established itself in Beira, Pemba and Chimoio. Procurement for Furniture, office supplies, Concluded and Furniture allocated.
4: Information Management and Reporting platform and mechanism estabnlished.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
